// Title: Group Membership Reconnaissance Via Whoami.EXE
// Sigma ID: bd8b828d-0dca-48e1-8a63-8a58ecf2644f
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-02-28 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: discovery, T1033
// Description: Detects the execution of whoami.exe with the /group command line flag to show group membership
//   for the current user, account type, security identifiers (SID), and attributes.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/whoami
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ad147b5514596e70f2782769d9833046b7c8e12b/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_whoami_groups_discovery.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\whoami.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "whoami.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains " /groups" or ProcessCommandLine contains " -groups")
